                <pb facs="0834" n="820" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg820"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Harlow, United
                        States marshal, to Mr. Fish, Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Marshal’s Office,
                            Southern District of New York</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">New
                            York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1869-11-08"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">November</hi> 8, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I am
                    employing, the same as my predecessor, General Barlow, one superintendent and
                    two or three detectives, (as circumstances require,) to learn of any
                    infringements of the neutrality law.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. R. HARLOW,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Marshal.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamilton Fish</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
